        allocution: "\"The foreman told me to drive that pickup because no one else was on the crew that morning. I know my license was revoked, and I should have said no even though I needed the job. I'm sorry for putting my employer in a bad spot. I'll handle my license before I drive anything else.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} told the foreman the license was fine.", "The foreman had been told about the revocation and drove {DL} to the job site the week before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you drive with a revoked license?", "\"I did, because my foreman told me to. He needed the truck moved, and no one else was there.\""), .direct("Did you tell him your license was revoked?", "\"I told him once, and he said it was fine. He said no one would check.\""), .direct("Why did you do it?", "\"I needed the job. I couldn't afford to lose it, so I drove.\""), .direct("Did you know it was illegal?", "\"Yes. I knew I shouldn't. I let him push me.\""), .direct("What did you do at the checkpoint?", "\"I told the trooper the truth, and I gave my real name.\""), .direct("What would you tell the trooper?", "\"I'm sorry for driving, and I should have refused when the foreman asked.\""), .cross("You've been convicted of driving while revoked before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I told the court I'd never drive again. I did, for my job.\""), .cross("Your foreman is the one who told you to drive?", "\"He is the one who told me to drive, and I'll tell the court his name.\""), .cross("You could have refused?", "\"I could have refused, and I'll refuse from now on, even if I lose the job.\""), .cross("You'll arrange another way to work?", "\"Yes, I'll arrange another way to get to work, with a ride or the bus.\""), .cross("You'll pay the fees to reinstate your license?", "\"Yes, I'll pay the fees to reinstate my license, as soon as I can.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} drove a company pickup through a safety checkpoint at 6:50 a.m., and the license check showed a revocation. {DL} came before this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}, and the revocation record is in evidence.", "The defense will say the boss told {D} to drive because no one else was on the crew that morning. {D} drove only because the job required it."),
        closings: ("The license check at the checkpoint shows a revocation, {D} was driving a company pickup, and with {PRIOR} already on {D.his} record, {DL} knew exactly what the revocation means.", "An order from a boss does not make the driving lawful. The State must prove {D} knew the license was revoked and drove anyway."),
        timeline: [(0, "6:50 a.m.: the checkpoint stop."), (0, "6:55 a.m.: the license check returns revoked."), (2, "The company turns over its log.")],
        identified: "Stopped at the scene.",
        notDone: ["The foreman's account of what {DL} told the foreman was never recorded."],
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let constructionZoneSpeed = SmallCases.make(
